%% Kaur Khor automations benchmark architecture.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Bench as Automations benchmark<br/>tests/bench/scenarios/automations.bench.ts
  participant Seed as Automation seed helper
  participant Route as Automations route
  participant Provider as AutomationProvider
  participant Dialog as AutomationIntakeDrawer
  participant Preload as Preload automation bridge
  participant Main as Electron main IPC
  participant Core as Managed desktop-core pool
  participant Store as SQLite automation<br/>and catalog rows
  participant Metrics as Benchmark summary

  Bench->>Metrics: wait for renderer.workspace.ready
  Bench->>Seed: ensure exposed catalog rows and intakes
  Seed->>Preload: automation seed writes
  Preload->>Main: IPC automation commands
  Main->>Core: mutation commands route to writer
  Core->>Store: write connection, exposure, intake state
  Store-->>Core: seed summary
  Core-->>Bench: exposed/intake row counts
  Bench->>Metrics: record benchmark.phase.seed_end
  Bench->>Metrics: record benchmark.phase.measurement_start

  Bench->>Route: navigate to /automations
  Route->>Provider: load workspace, connection, catalog exposure, intakes
  Provider->>Preload: automation.getWorkspace and related reads
  Preload->>Metrics: record preload.invoke.* spans
  Preload->>Main: IPC read commands
  Main->>Core: coalesced read-only commands
  Core->>Store: read automation and catalog rows
  Store-->>Core: route data
  Core-->>Provider: route data
  Provider-->>Route: hydrated automation workspace
  Route->>Metrics: record route.automations.ready

  Bench->>Route: switch Catalog tab and exposure filters
  Route->>Metrics: record interaction.automations_exposure_filter_ms
  Bench->>Route: switch Live intake tab
  Route->>Metrics: record interaction.automations_live_intake_table_ms
  Bench->>Dialog: open intake drawer
  Dialog->>Provider: read selected intake and conversation
  Provider->>Preload: automation.readConversation
  Preload->>Main: IPC read conversation
  Main->>Core: read-only route command
  Core->>Store: intake detail rows
  Store-->>Dialog: conversation detail
  Dialog->>Metrics: record interaction.open_automation_intake_drawer_ms

  Bench->>Route: switch Needs review tab
  Route->>Metrics: record interaction.automations_exceptions_section_ms
  Bench->>Metrics: record benchmark.phase.measurement_end
  Bench->>Metrics: evaluate automations target coverage

  Note over Route,Provider: The route is tab-driven and measures connection, catalog exposure, live intake, drawer, and exceptions surfaces
  Note over Main,Core: Automation writes use the writer while route reads may use read workers
